WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.303
-Our next guest is an Emmy and
Golden Globe-nominated actress

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.538
and producer you know from
her work on films like

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:06.973
"Mank" and "Rules Don't Apply."

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:10.142
She stars in the third season of
"Emily in Paris," which begins

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:12.111
streaming on Netflix
December 21st.

00:00:12.111 --> 00:00:13.212
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:16.148
-Bonjour, it's Emily in Paris.

00:00:16.148 --> 00:00:19.118
Today is day one of
funemployment.

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:22.355
I want to know where and what
you guys want to see.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:27.526
I am your eyes and ears
to this beautiful city.

00:00:27.526 --> 00:00:29.795
Wow, oh. A lot of you are
joining already.

00:00:29.795 --> 00:00:31.264
Okay, let's see here.

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:34.333
"I want to see Monet's
'Water Lilies.'" So do I.

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:37.503
"Can you try Angelina's
hot chocolate?

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:40.973
I do not need an excuse
for that, so yes, I will.

00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:44.110
And "Go back to --
go back to America."

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.713
No, I think we're done here
for now, alright?

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:51.851
But my DMs are open and I will
see you there, mwah, merci!

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:54.754
-Please welcome back to the show
Lily Collins, everybody!

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.389
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:56.389 --> 00:01:05.064 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:13.739 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:13.739 --> 00:01:15.741
I am so happy to have you here.

00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:17.843
-I am so happy to be back.

00:01:17.843 --> 00:01:19.779
-This is very exciting.
We did not know this, and I will

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:21.147
admit to have not seen the film,

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:23.349
but you and Paul Bettany worked
together before.

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:26.085
-We did. It was my second film,
yeah, called "Priest."

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:27.486
-Called "Priest."

00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:30.389
It was described on Google
as a sci-fi vampire thriller.

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:32.091
Is that --
-I mean, that feels very

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:34.360
appropriate for about
eight years ago.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.628
They were very in at the time.

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:37.029
-It was a lot of vampire stuff.

00:01:37.029 --> 00:01:38.564
-There was a lot of
vampire stuff.

00:01:38.564 --> 00:01:39.865
-And here is a real good shot.

00:01:39.865 --> 00:01:44.470
Obviously this is a very sort of
heady, dialogue-driven --

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:45.872
-Yes, very.
-Chamber piece,

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.774
and here's a picture of you
and Paul. There you are.

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:51.177
-And look, that's --
that face says it all.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:53.613
I mean, I think this was
like my third day on set.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:54.947
-Well, there you go.
-Yeah.

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:57.950
-Very natural. You definitely
seem to be concerned.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:59.451
-Flailing, I like to say.

00:01:59.451 --> 00:02:01.754
-A lot has happened since you
were last year.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:04.790
Engaged, married, celebrated
your one-year anniversary,

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.559
congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:08.460
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.230
Yeah, a lot happened in COVID.
-A lot happened in COVID.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.900
One of the nice things about
sort of being in

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.101
this side of it, especially with
"Emily in Paris,"

00:02:16.101 --> 00:02:17.970
this is a show people enjoyed
a great deal during COVID.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.705
But we were talking backstage,
this is the first time you've

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:21.574
actually been able to be out
and promoting it

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:23.009
and see your cast off the set.

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.343
-Yeah. It's crazy.

00:02:24.343 --> 00:02:26.913
Also to be back in rooms like
this with an audience,

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.147
with you, it's so nice.

00:02:28.147 --> 00:02:30.049
We never really got to celebrate
together,

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:32.284
and all of a sudden
it feels real.

00:02:32.284 --> 00:02:33.686
You know when something
comes out

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:36.021
and all you're seeing is
stats and numbers.

00:02:36.021 --> 00:02:37.289
And you're like,
"I think it's hitting?

00:02:37.289 --> 00:02:39.125
I don't know,
I think people like it?"

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:40.760
Now you get to have the
interactions

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.629
and celebrate
and it feels really special.

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:45.665
-It is really special, and it's
really cool to have it back on.

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:48.467
You have a costar in the show,
Bruno,

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:50.369
who is also one of the stars of
"White Lotus."

00:02:50.369 --> 00:02:53.305
-I know!
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:53.305 --> 00:02:56.809
-It was very nice to see him
turn up in both.

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:58.611
Have you caught up
on "White Lotus"?

00:02:58.611 --> 00:03:00.179
-I have not yet caught up.

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:01.547
Unfortunately,
I haven't had time.

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:03.616
You know, World Cup
has also been on.

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.852
I'm so sorry to say,
but it's been like

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.386
"Emily" press and World Cup.

00:03:07.386 --> 00:03:10.022
But I'm very excited
to support Bruno,

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:12.958
and I loved season one,
so I'm very excited.

00:03:12.958 --> 00:03:14.627
-Well, I won't give anything
away.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.029
It turns out great for him.

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:17.763
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.763 --> 00:03:20.532
-I've heard little spoilers
already.

00:03:20.532 --> 00:03:22.101
-Wait, World Cup now,

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:25.304
I know we're down to
France and Argentina.

00:03:25.304 --> 00:03:28.341
Is "Emily in Paris" loyalty here
making you root for France?

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:30.709
-I mean, we were just in Paris
promoting a show

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:33.012
and there was a game, and all of
us running from room to room

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.981
in our PJs, being like,
"The game's on!"

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.782
They're like, "We got to get
ready for the premiere!"

00:03:36.782 --> 00:03:38.851
And everyone's like,
"What do we choose?"

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:42.921
But it's been really fun
to support and cheer on.

00:03:42.921 --> 00:03:45.024
Charlie and I both love watching
it. It's so fun.

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:47.326
-I've been lucky enough to know
your husband over the years.

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:49.628
I also know his parents.
You have very good in-laws.

00:03:49.628 --> 00:03:51.464
I'm lucky. I have good in-laws
as well.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:54.233
Is this is something that you
recognized early on,

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:56.135
that you hit the jackpot?
-Yeah.

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.436
Oh, my God, are you kidding?

00:03:57.436 --> 00:04:01.574
Mary, Ted, Malcolm -- I'm so
fortunate for my in-laws.

00:04:02.808 --> 00:04:05.644
I think I actually met Mary
and Ted before I met Charlie,

00:04:05.644 --> 00:04:06.846
which was interesting.

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:07.880
We danced together.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.148
-Oh, wow.
-Yeah.

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:10.816
-This is Ted Danson
and Mary Steenburgen.

00:04:10.816 --> 00:04:13.519
You got to work with Ted
on an episode of "Curb."

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.087
-I did.
-More importantly, you got to

00:04:15.087 --> 00:04:16.889
work with Larry --
I mean, Ted's great, I love Ted.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:18.891
But you got to do a scene with
Larry David.

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:23.162
-Yeah, it was like a fleeting
10 to 20 seconds where we just

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:25.531
freaked out at each other,
which was so fun.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:26.766
We just like screamed
at each other.

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:29.335
-You did.
I went back and watched.

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:31.303
If memory served, when I was
thinking about it today,

00:04:31.303 --> 00:04:33.139
I don't think it's very long
that they spent together.

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:34.507
But you got the full Larry.

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:36.108
-Guys.
-[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.108 --> 00:04:39.278
That is the most important
freeze frame

00:04:39.278 --> 00:04:40.913
you'll ever see of me.

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:43.483
I think that that's the most --
I mean, it literally was just

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:45.918
like "aaaah" the whole time.

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:47.286
And it was all improv.

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:50.289
I guess I can "aaaah" improv
really well, I don't know.

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:51.624
-You can scream improv.

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:53.426
-I scream with Paul
flying off a train

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:54.860
and I can do it with Larry.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.328
-They saw "Priest"
and they were like,

00:04:56.328 --> 00:04:59.165
"I think if she's as good
as she was there."

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:01.967
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.967 --> 00:05:04.470
-Same outfit too.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.438
-How do you find out
that you're going to be

00:05:06.438 --> 00:05:08.941
in an episode of "Curb"?
Do you just get a phone call?

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:12.511
-Yeah, actually, weirdly I was
up shooting "Windfall,"

00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:15.948
a movie I did with Charlie,
and it was my 32nd birthday.

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:19.785
I got a phone call saying that
Larry David wants you in "Curb."

00:05:19.785 --> 00:05:21.420
And I was like, "Why?

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:22.888
Why me? What?"

00:05:22.888 --> 00:05:24.690
I had known his daughter Cazzie
for a while,

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:26.592
and I assumed it was that,
and it was like,

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:29.662
no, they have a storyline about
you and "Emily in Paris."

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:33.232
I just thought
that was so random.

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:35.968
And amazing because
I'm a huge fan.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:38.070
And yeah, it was
kind of surreal.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:40.105
And I found out -- It was weird,
actually.

00:05:40.105 --> 00:05:42.175
I found out on my 30th birthday

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:43.943
that I was going to be
in "Emily in Paris."

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:45.611
And then on my 32nd birthday,

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:47.246
I found out I was going to be
in "Curb."

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:50.216
On my 20th birthday I found out
I'd be in my first movie,

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:52.652
"The Blind Side." I'm like,
what's going to happen at 40?

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:53.986
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:56.022
-I think it's going to be
"Priest 2" with Paul Bettany.

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:57.189
-Yes!

00:05:57.189 --> 00:05:59.291
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:59.291 --> 00:06:01.861
I am down. I am down.

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:07.066
-So your costar, Ashley Park,
you guys actually live,

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:08.534
basically, in the same building
in Paris

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:09.735
where you're shooting the show.

00:06:09.735 --> 00:06:12.237
-We did. This is the first year
that we lived in

00:06:12.237 --> 00:06:14.173
the same building,
which was so much fun.

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:15.975
It was basically
life imitating art.

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:19.978
And every day we'd either, like,
run up to each other's

00:06:19.978 --> 00:06:23.049
apartments, we'd, like, do lines
together -- Whoa, whoa.

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:26.752
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.752 --> 00:06:28.921
We would run lines together.
-Yeah.

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:30.489
Yeah, yeah.
We call it "run lines."

00:06:30.489 --> 00:06:31.924
-Yeah, okay.
-[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:34.026
-Yeah.

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:36.095
-Correction.

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:38.230
We, like, played Mario Kart
together.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:39.631
We'd talk about life.

00:06:39.631 --> 00:06:43.936
And we'd go on adventures around
the city, scootering, bicycling.

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:47.306
-This is like a photo
from a mystery novel.

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:48.741
Because this is a photo that...
-Oh, my God.

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:51.577
-...was taken by Ashley
at a flea market.

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:54.246
And there's something that's
happening in this moment.

00:06:54.246 --> 00:06:57.950
-No one here will ever know.
But I will tell you.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:06:59.452
Okay, so we're at a flea market.

00:06:59.452 --> 00:07:03.589
And this is a selfie that Ashley
took in a mirror, which --

00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:06.592
It's very telling of all three
of us in this photo.

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:10.696
Ashley loves to, you know, take
photos wherever we go to,

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:11.997
like, create memories
and have it.

00:07:11.997 --> 00:07:14.200
Charlie is being inquisitive,
as one should,

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.568
talking to the artist
where we are.

00:07:15.568 --> 00:07:18.471
And I'm feverishly
touching my tooth,

00:07:18.471 --> 00:07:21.807
realizing I just chipped
my entire front tooth

00:07:21.807 --> 00:07:25.378
and I have to film a close-up
on Monday, and it's Saturday.

00:07:25.378 --> 00:07:30.249
And we're in France, where
things are...a lot of the time.

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:32.418
And finding a dentist
on a Sunday

00:07:32.418 --> 00:07:33.853
would be nearly impossible.

00:07:33.853 --> 00:07:37.322
But per Emily's solution-driven
nature, I found a dentist.

00:07:37.322 --> 00:07:39.191
-Wow.
-On a Sunday morning who had

00:07:39.191 --> 00:07:42.028
been out the night before
at the Rolling Stones concert.

00:07:42.028 --> 00:07:43.528
[ Laughter ]

00:07:43.528 --> 00:07:47.333
And bicycled to the office, let
me in, didn't really scrub up,

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:50.402
then I lay on the table and he's
like, "Let me fix your tooth."

00:07:50.402 --> 00:07:52.104
I was like, "Okay!"

00:07:52.104 --> 00:07:54.473
And he did a great job,
and he didn't charge me.

00:07:54.473 --> 00:07:57.043
-Wow.
-I was a win-win.

00:07:57.043 --> 00:07:59.312
-That's a real "Emily in Paris"
storyline.

00:07:59.312 --> 00:08:01.246
Do you remember
how you chipped it?

00:08:01.246 --> 00:08:04.683
-I was eating an apple
in the back of a taxi.

00:08:04.683 --> 00:08:06.719
-Une pomme?
-Une pomme. Yes.

00:08:06.719 --> 00:08:08.253
[ Laughter ]

00:08:08.253 --> 00:08:10.889
Une pomme which I will never,
ever do again.

00:08:10.889 --> 00:08:13.559
-Pas du pomme.
-Pas du pomme.

00:08:13.559 --> 00:08:15.995
No, not good.

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:18.130
-My mom was a French teacher,
so that's why.

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:20.566
-It's very impressive.
-Comes pretty naturally to me.

00:08:20.566 --> 00:08:22.535
[ Laughter ]

00:08:22.535 --> 00:08:24.369
-There is something that
happened,

00:08:24.369 --> 00:08:26.772
I guess in your writers room,
that happens on the show

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:28.808
this year, which is a pigeon
gets in the office.

00:08:28.808 --> 00:08:31.210
-Yeah, I mean, has that never
happened to you?

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:33.679
-It has happened to us.
We had a pigeon in our office.

00:08:33.679 --> 00:08:35.481
-Oh, really? Oh, my God!

00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:38.650
-We have pigeons in our office
like pretty much all the time.

00:08:38.650 --> 00:08:40.218
-I mean, we're in New York.
I get it.

00:08:40.218 --> 00:08:42.054
-We are in New York.
-I get it.

00:08:42.054 --> 00:08:43.823
-Did you get to actually work
with them?

00:08:43.823 --> 00:08:45.524
-We did.
-Professional pigeons?

00:08:45.524 --> 00:08:47.727
-Guys, pigeons are
some of the hardest cast

00:08:47.727 --> 00:08:49.828
to wrangle and they're
the most expensive.

00:08:49.828 --> 00:08:52.231
-Really? The pigeons cost more
than on other actors?

00:08:52.231 --> 00:08:53.666
-They come with wranglers.
-Okay.

00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:55.568
-And there are multiple
kinds of pigeons.

00:08:55.568 --> 00:08:57.436
There are the trained
flight pigeons

00:08:57.436 --> 00:08:59.138
and there are the wild pigeons.

00:08:59.138 --> 00:09:02.608
And in this, in episode 3, you
see we get to deal with both.

00:09:02.608 --> 00:09:05.277
-Really?
-We had a clear flight plan

00:09:05.277 --> 00:09:07.345
for these pigeons to go through.
-Uh-huh.

00:09:07.345 --> 00:09:08.580
-And they just didn't.

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:10.549
And what they used in the show

00:09:10.549 --> 00:09:13.018
was real-life moments of them
going rogue.

00:09:13.018 --> 00:09:15.888
-I feel like you definitely want
to throw in

00:09:15.888 --> 00:09:21.126
the extra couple of euros to get
the trained pigeons

00:09:21.126 --> 00:09:22.394
as opposed to the wild pigeons.

00:09:22.394 --> 00:09:24.130
-I know. One would think.

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:26.098
But they were landing
all over the place.

00:09:26.098 --> 00:09:28.700
They didn't speak French.
They didn't speak English.

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:30.135
They didn't speak pigeon.

00:09:30.135 --> 00:09:31.938
They just, like, did
their own thing.

00:09:31.938 --> 00:09:36.442
And all the takes that they used
are of Kate Walsh and I trying

00:09:36.442 --> 00:09:39.144
our hardest not to crack a smile
or laugh

00:09:39.144 --> 00:09:41.747
and just screaming at them
in whatever language we could.

00:09:41.747 --> 00:09:43.148
-Yeah.
-To get them to move.

00:09:43.148 --> 00:09:45.117
-This seems very similar to
your work with Larry David.

00:09:45.117 --> 00:09:46.986
You just had to scream.
-[ Laughter ]

00:09:46.986 --> 00:09:50.456
-I'm so good at that.
I just -- Yeah.

00:09:50.456 --> 00:09:51.790
-Well, thank you so much
for being here.

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:53.426
Congratulations on season three.
-Thank you.

00:09:53.426 --> 00:09:54.660
-We're always so happy
when you stop by.

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:57.062
-I love being here.
-You guys, Lily Collins.

00:09:57.062 --> 00:09:59.131
The third season of
"Emily in Paris"

00:09:59.131 --> 00:10:01.300
begins streaming December 31st
on Netflix.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:02.902
We'll be right back with more
"Late Night."

